{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2021-07-28 11:30:00', 'title': "STATE'S GRID OPERATOR ASKS CALIFORNIANS TO CONSERVE ENERGY TODAY DUE TO HIGH ENERGY DEMAND AND TIGHT SUPPLIES ACROSS THE WEST", 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--WITH HIGHER THAN NORMAL TEMPERATURES FORECAST IN SOME PARTS OF CALIFORNIA TODAY, THE STATE'S POWER GRID OPERATOR IS ASKING RESIDENTS STATEWIDE TO VOLUNTARILY CONSERVE ELECTRICITY THIS AFTERNOON AND EVENING WHEN THE GRID IS MOST STRESSED DUE TO HIGHER DEMAND AND ENERGY SUPPLIES ARE TIGHTER. THE FLEX ALERT, CALLED BY THE CALIFORNIA INDEPENDENT SYSTEM OPERATOR (CAISO), WAS ISSUED YESTERDAY AND WILL BE IN EFFECT TODAY FROM 4 P.M. TO 9 P.M. THE GRID OPERATOR IS PREDIC"}